  "caption": "Quinn rolled over in bed at 6am and the whole room spun. Sitting still, it settled within a minute, then came back when reaching for the top shelf.\n\nBrief dizziness set off by certain head positions can be BPPV: tiny crystals in the inner ear drift into a balance canal, so head movements send false spinning signals.\n\nWhat often helps: get the right diagnosis first (which ear and canal matter), then a guided repositioning manoeuvre like the Epley. Feeling briefly dizzy during it, and a bit unsteady for a day or two after, is common. It can come back, and the same approach often helps again.\n\nConstant vertigo, a new severe headache, double vision, slurred speech, weakness or hearing loss need prompt medical assessment.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
